# CW3002 and nothing else. The consumer declares `eat`, which the library
# exports, and gives it a DIFFERENT parameter mode: the library borrows, the
# consumer consumes. Shadowing an export is legal and warns.
#
# The library's own `drive` calls the library's own `eat`. That call is the
# library author's code and the consumer cannot edit it, so it must be measured
# against the library's declaration. Measuring it against the winner of the name
# made the library's body hear CE2427 and CE2405 about source the consumer never
# wrote (#487, section 13.1 of docs/design/unit-namespaces.md).
# EXPECT_ERROR_CODE: CW3002

use <collections/strings>
use <lib/shadow_modes_lib>

fn eat(nom string s) i32:
    return Result.Ok(s.len() * 2)

fn main() i32:
    let string msg = "answer"
    println("{eat(nom msg).realise(0)}")
    println("{drive().realise(0)}")
    return Result.Ok(0)
